# CODEOWNERS — the registry catalog + the locked decision artifacts have a real owner on record.
# This is the ownership half of ADR-0021's trust model: registry/index.json is CI-built, and the
# `registry-index` byte-identical rebuild (a REQUIRED status check on `main`) blocks a hand-edit.
#
# ENFORCEMENT (live): branch protection on `main` requires the `check`, `standards-gate`, and
# `registry-index` status checks + blocks force-push/deletion. "Require review from Code Owners" is
# intentionally NOT enabled — this is a single-owner account, so a code-owner-review gate would block
# self-merge with no second approver. Re-enable it the moment a second collaborator joins.

# The generator allowlist — CI-built from the ledger; no hand-edits without owner review (ADR-0021).
/registry/index.json            @GridWork-dev
# The version ledger — the index's sole source of truth; a gated publish appends here (CI, P5).
/registry/ledger.jsonl          @GridWork-dev

# Locked decision artifacts (CLAUDE.md source-of-truth #1 + #2).
/knowledge/decisions/           @GridWork-dev
/docs/state/decisions-and-forks.md  @GridWork-dev

# The standards gate itself — changing the gate changes what's enforceable.
/tooling/                       @GridWork-dev
/.dependency-cruiser.cjs        @GridWork-dev
/.github/                       @GridWork-dev
